            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0656" n="560" xml:id="pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/2820: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-04T18:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">October 4,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:55
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>45. Yesterday a new uprising occupied Telica and Somotillo. The Government has
                    sent approximately 600 men there for the purpose of quelling this uprising. The
                    President is exasperated believing that Honduranean authorities are not acting
                    in good faith with him, failing to take necessary measures to prevent recurrence
                    of invasion of this country.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
